 "comment": "creditor_ageing_43bh, vouchers that share a GUID (#1243). A micro creditor with an opening balance partly paid: one GUID on a bill and on its payment (both cited) and on a voucher that touches no creditor (not cited), a blank-GUID bill and a blank-GUID payment, one GUID, number, type and day on two bills (one ref, both walked), a blank-GUID voucher billing two creditors, and a blank-GUID voucher whose line is nil (not cited). A small creditor with an unpaid opening balance, a bill whose ref is identical to the micro creditor's two (the opening-dues finding cites it once) and the two-creditor voucher. An unclassified creditor with blank-GUID bills whose numbers differ only in case, and one GUID on bills numbered with a letter, an accented letter composed and decomposed, a full-width letter and a character beyond U+FFFF. A trader: one GUID on a bill and on a payment over it. The canonical dump sorts refs itself, so this golden does not pin the order the module emits them in.",
